==Battleground==
*20 [[Brollow]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Dogenstein]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.
*1 [[Dark Dober]] spawns as the boss after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*10 [[Celeboodle]]s spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Tarsiriel]] spawns after 93.33 seconds<sup>2,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage debuts Dark Dober, who necessitates the use of specific counters thanks to his abilities. Unfortunately for you, Dark Dober comes packed with extremely high health as well as Weakening Mini-Waves that further extend his health. Combine this with his Sage trait, this means that most counters to Dark enemies like [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] or [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] won't work. Your best bet to counter Dark Dober is to either use a [[Talents|Talented]] [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]] or just spam Talented [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]].

This stage in particular demonstrates just how dangerous Dark Dober can be. Normally, you could just lure Dark Dober and jump him with Dark Lazer, but the presence of Tarsiriel complicates this hard. The Brollows thrive off of Dark Lazer's weak Waves, while Celeboodle ruins any plans for you to use [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]]. Try to get [[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]] to nuke the Brollows. Given how this stage plays out, you're not going to have the luxury of using [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Soractes]] for Tarsiriel, so try your best to time units out of Tarsiriel's range. Don't forget to run [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] for Dogenstein as well.

